From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:49:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246: Add the
 bootloader's ids
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Not for upstream: the binding allows qcom,msm-id and qcom,board-id on
older SoCs only, and lets this board through here.

The bootloader picks a tree out of the vendor_boot dtb area by these
two properties. This port gives it a dtbo it cannot parse, so that no
overlay is applied, and on that path it uses the strict matcher, which
keeps a tree only if every field equals the board's. The values are
what the phone reports in /sys/devices/soc0: SoC 537 at revision 1.0,
grouped with 613 as the stock base tree groups them, and a QRD at
platform version 1.0, subtype 0. The DDR type is not reported, so the
board id is given once for each of the eight.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml      |  1 +
 .../dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts  | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml
index 1500a8fdf..5c742ab0e 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml
@@ -1191,6 +1191,7 @@ allOf:
               - qcom,sm6115
               - qcom,sm6125
               - qcom,sm6350
+              - qcom,sm6450
               - qcom,sm7125
               - qcom,sm7225
               - qcom,sm8150
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
index 741acd00d..41a2ff0fc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
@@ -25,6 +25,18 @@ / {
 	compatible = "sony,pdx246", "qcom,sm6450";
 	chassis-type = "handset";
 
+	/*
+	 * Not for upstream. The bootloader boots a tree from the vendor_boot
+	 * dtb area only if it carries these, and with no overlay it can read
+	 * it matches them exactly: SoC 537 or 613 at revision 1.0, and a QRD
+	 * at platform version 1.0, subtype 0, with any of the eight DDR types,
+	 * since the board does not report its own.
+	 */
+	qcom,msm-id = <537 0x10000>, <613 0x10000>;
+	qcom,board-id = <0x1000b 0x000>, <0x1000b 0x100>, <0x1000b 0x200>,
+			<0x1000b 0x300>, <0x1000b 0x400>, <0x1000b 0x500>,
+			<0x1000b 0x600>, <0x1000b 0x700>;
+
 	aliases {
 		serial0 = &uart3;
 		serial1 = &uart11;
